# MTG Builder Repository Overview

This repository provides a FastAPI deck editor and a FastMCP card-search server over MTGJSON card data.

## Runtime architecture

- `server.bat` / `src/server.py`: MCP stdio entry point and `plain_search_card`.
- `editor.bat` / `src/deck_editor/app.py`: deck editor HTTP API, SSE updates, recommendations, and synergy checker.
- `src/lib/cardDB.py`: canonical card/face resolution, exact structural filters, and GraphRAG integration.
- `src/obj/card.py`: card model, oracle parsing, and typed mechanic signatures.
- `src/lib/graphrag_build.py`: deterministic BYOG entities, relationships, text units, adjacency, and Commander Spellbook provenance.
- `src/lib/build_rag.py`: GraphRAG community detection, cached top-level reports, and deduplicated Gemini/LanceDB embeddings.
- `src/lib/graphrag_service.py`: validated runtime loading, semantic ranking, graph traversal, pair evidence, recommendation analysis, and exact cache invalidation.
- `src/lib/graphrag_benchmark.py`: frozen-baseline and representative-deck cutover gate.
- `data/graphrag/`: generated Parquet, manifest, reports, and LanceDB data.

## Retrieval behavior

- Exact CardDB filters remain authoritative for name, type, colors, mana value, legality, and price.
- General semantic search combines card embeddings, exact query-to-mechanic mappings, typed traversal, and MTGJSON EDHREC rank.
- Trigger/effect search maps known query phrases to typed mechanics; unknown phrases use mechanic embeddings before traversal.
- Recommendations are prevalidated by current deck format/color/copy rules, then combine graph evidence, deck embeddings, and popularity.
- Pair synergy and additions cite MTGJSON or Commander Spellbook evidence.
- Runtime loading fails unless manifest and artifact hashes validate.

## Commands

- `install.bat install`: create/update the Python 3.11 `mtg-rag` environment.
- `install.bat download`: fetch MTGJSON data.
- `install.bat build`: clean-build GraphRAG and LanceDB artifacts.
- `install.bat update`: refresh cards, prices, and the full index.
- `server.bat`: run MCP; `editor.bat`: run deck editor.

Use `src.utils.logger.LOGGER`, strict type hints, and fail-visible error handling.
